                <pb facs="0852" n="732" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg732"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Pearson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-10-04"><hi rendition="#italic">October 4,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis advises Mr. Pearson that no effective guaranty that this government
                    will protect Persian subjects can be given, but demand may be made upon the
                    Persian Government to give the necessary protection if there be ground to fear
                    miscarriage of justice through intimidation of the native witnesses in the
                    Labaree case.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
